# A download that stops receiving before it has a file name sat at "0 bytes" for good, and the file
# over the Library button (the bin) waited for it, over the sidebar's buttons and taking their
# clicks (GitHub #491). Holding Cra's answer to where it goes makes such a download: no file name,
# and ${TRICKLE} sends nothing after its first 64 KB. Until the bin has a file, its edge leaves
# clicks to what is under it; 30 s without a byte later, the bin goes.
# promise: #491
home
budget rss=600 stalls50=5
env CRA_TEST_HOLD_DOWNLOAD_DESTINATION=1
cra://open?url=${PAGE}
wait 2
cra://open?url=${TRICKLE}/trickle.bin
wait 3
cra://debug?downloadState=held
expect-log Download [0-9]+ started: no file name yet
expect-log download state held: running=true .* bin=shown \(no file\), its edge hits [A-Z]
# The download the person started holds every guard: ⌘Q asks, the automatic update restart waits and Install and
# Relaunch asks. The readout below must say so, or its "none" in web-store-install-quit-guards proves nothing.
cra://debug?downloadGuards=held
expect-log download guards held: quit=downloads in progress autoUpdate=a download is in progress installAndRelaunch=asks$
wait 37
cra://debug?downloadState=stuck
expect-log Download [0-9]+ stuck for 30 s: no file name yet
expect-log download state stuck: running=true .* bin=none
cra://debug?downloadDestination=cancel
wait 2
cra://debug?downloadState=cancelled
expect-log download state cancelled: running=false progress=none rows=\["Cancelled"\] bin=none
cra://debug?downloadGuards=cancelled
expect-log download guards cancelled: quit=none autoUpdate=none installAndRelaunch=none$
